  "english": "24. Thursday. Feast of Triphon, Barsamas, and Onuphrius the hermits.\n26. Saturday. Feast of Athanasius and Cyril the Patriarchs.\n27. Sunday. Second. [Tone 2] Barekendan [Pre-Lenten Eve] of the Fast of Catechumens. For the others, see the First Volume up to Vardavar [Transfiguration], keeping the order of this place.\nSee further below.\n4. Monday. Feast of the Atomian Generals, and Bishop Mark, Pion, and the others.\n11. Monday. Feast of the Vardanian Generals.\n14. Thursday. Presentation of the Lord [Tearndaraj].\n17. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK / ԴԿ]. Great Barekendan [Eve of Great Lent]. See also the others according to their order in the First Volume.\nApril\n7. Sunday. Tone 1 [ADz / ԱՁ]. Easter [Zatik], Day of the Resurrection of Christ, and the Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin.\nMay\n16. Thursday. Tone 8 [DK / ԴԿ]. Ascension of Christ.\n26. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK / ԱԿ]. Coming of the Holy Spirit [Pentecost]. Barekendan of the Elijah Fast.\nJune\n2. Sunday. Tone 1 [ADz / ԱՁ]. First. Beginning of the Sundays of the Resurrection. Canticle [Harts] God: \"Who came for salvation\" (Որ եկիր ի փրկութիւն).\nJuly\n14. Sunday. Tone 3 [BDz / ԲՁ]. Vardavar [Transfiguration]. The period of non-fasting [utikh] is four weeks. See in the First Volume up to the Friday and Saturday of the third week which is here; but look here for the Sunday Canticles [Harts].\n21. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK / ԱԿ]. Second. Canticle [Harts] Tone 3 [BDz / ԲՁ]: \"Who descended from heaven, without beginning\" (Որ ի յերկնից իջեր անսկիզբն).\n28. Sunday. Tone 1 [ADz / ԱՁ]. Third. Canticle [Harts] Tone 6 [GK / ԳԿ]: \"Who of the heavenly hosts\" (Որ երկնային զինուորութեանցդ). And see the others according to their order.\nAugust\n3. Saturday. Tone 7 [DDz / ԴՁ]. Feast of Gregory the Theologian.\n4. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK / ԴԿ]. Fourth. Canticle [Harts] Tone 7 [DDz / ԴՁ]: \"We glorify\" (Փառաւորեմք).\n5. Monday. Tone 1 [ADz / ԱՁ]. Feast of Eugene [Eugenios], Macarius, and the others. Canticle [Harts] Tone 7 [DDz / ԴՁ]: \"Holy art Thou, Lord of hosts\" (Սուրբ ես տէր զօրութեանց). But know this: if a leap year occurs and the year-letter is Ղ, Ձ, or Չ, do not celebrate Eugene and Macarius here, because they are celebrated in the first year-letter after the Nativity, as you can see; instead of them, celebrate Abraham, Khoren, and Astvatsatur, who are placed below under the virgin Juliana. But in other years, celebrate without hesitation as it is written.\n6. Wednesday. Tone 2 [AK / ԱԿ]. Feast of Andrew the General and his army, and the others.\n8. Thursday. Tone 4 [BK / ԲԿ]. Feast of Adrian [Adrianos] and his wife Anatolia, and the others. Canticle [Harts] Tone 8 [DK / ԴԿ]: \"To Thee, O God\" (Առ քեզ աստուած).\n10. Saturday. Tone 6 [GK / ԳԿ]. Feast of the holy ecumenical Council of Ephesus, the two hundred Patriarchs.\n11. Sunday. Tone 7 [DDz / ԴՁ]. Fifth. Canticle [Harts] Tone 6 [GK / ԳԿ]: \"Ineffable\" (Անճառելի). Barekendan of the Fast of the Holy Mother of God.\n12. Monday. Tone 8 [DK / ԴԿ]. Fast of the Holy Mother of God. Canticle of Fasting [Harts aghts] Tone 3 [BDz / ԲՁ]: \"Who saved\" (Որ ապրեցու).\n18. Sunday. Tone 6 [GK / ԳԿ]. Assumption [Verapokhum] of the Holy Mother of God. The period of non-fasting [utikh] is three weeks. See this period in the First Volume, keeping the order of this place.\nSeptember\n8. Sunday. Tone 3 [BDz / ԲՁ]. Fourth. Feast of the Birth of the Holy Mother of God from Anna. Barekendan of the Holy Cross.\n9. Monday. Tone 4 [BK / ԲԿ]. Fast of the Holy Cross. Canticle of Fasting [Harts aghts] Tone 4 [BK / ԲԿ]: \"Lord God of our fathers\" (Տէր աստուած հարցն մերոց).\n15. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK / ԱԿ]. Exaltation of the Holy Cross [Khachverats]. See up to the tenth Sunday in the First Volume, keeping the order of this place.\n22. Sunday. Tone 1 [ADz / ԱՁ]. Second. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 1 [ADz / ԱՁ]: \"With the women\" (Ընդ կանայսն). Barekendan of the Cross of Varag.",
